    {
      "block_id": "2605.06070_p17_b1",
      "text": "A natural question is whether the performance gains of ArenaPO can also be achieved by introducing\nan explicit reward model, similar to RLHF-style optimization. Following this suggestion, we augment\nDiffusion-DPO with ImageReward as an explicit reward model and compare it against ArenaPO.\n",
      "bbox": [
        107.64,
        97.6,
        504.0,
        129.3
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        430,
        390,
        2016,
        517
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.86,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 289,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.06070_p17_b2",
      "text": "The results are presented in Table 8. Incorporating ImageReward substantially improves the IR metric\nitself, indicating that the model tends to optimize specifically toward the reward model objective.\nHowever, improvements on other evaluation metrics remain limited and generally do not surpass\nArenaPO. In some cases, such as HPS, the performance even degrades compared with ArenaPO.\nSimilar observations have also been reported in the Diffusion-DPO paper [35], which notes that \u201cwe\ndid not observe stable improvement when training from public implementations on Pick-a-Pic.\u201d\n",
      "bbox": [
        107.64,
        135.8,
        505.75,
        200.06
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        430,
